# speech2speech configuration. Copy to .env and edit, then `docker compose up -d`.
# Every value below is read by the containers, none is baked into an image.

# ============================== Models ==============================
# Any OpenAI compatible endpoint: a self hosted server (Ollama, vLLM, LM Studio,
# a server at your institution) or a hosted API. Nothing leaves your network when
# the endpoint is your own. The base URL may be given with or without /v1.

# Chat model. Mandatory. It does the translating.
LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
LLM_MODEL=your-model
LLM_API_KEY=

# Speech to text. Mandatory for talking, a Whisper style model. Without it the
# page still translates what you type and says that the microphone has no model.
# Base URL and key fall back to the LLM values, the model never does.
STT_MODEL=your-speech-to-text-model
#STT_BASE_URL=
#STT_API_KEY=

# Speech output. Optional, reads a translation aloud. Needs both the model and a
# voice name the endpoint knows. There is no default voice, because voice names
# differ per server and most refuse a name they do not know. Without both the
# page shows no read aloud button.
#TTS_MODEL=your-text-to-speech-model
#TTS_VOICE=your-voice
#TTS_BASE_URL=
#TTS_API_KEY=

# Last fallback for every API key above.
#OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ============================== Access ==============================
# One password for everybody who opens the page. Unset means no password at all,
# which is fine on a network only you can reach. Set it before you publish the page.
#ACCESS_PASSWORD=

# Signs the access cookie. Any long random string, for example `openssl rand -hex 32`.
# Unset derives it from the password, so changing the password signs everybody out.
#SESSION_SECRET=

# ============================== Limits ==============================
# Conversations kept at once. A new one past this pushes the one untouched longest out.
#MAX_SESSIONS=100
# Characters one conversation may collect, spoken and typed together. Reaching it
# ends the conversation, it stays readable and nothing is cut away.
#SESSION_CHAR_LIMIT=20000
# Largest recording one request may carry, in bytes. A larger one is refused, never cut.
#MAX_AUDIO_BYTES=31457280
# Characters per request to the speech model. Longer text is split at sentence ends.
#TTS_MAX_CHARS_PER_REQUEST=400

# ============================== Storage =============================
# The SQLite file with the conversations. A named volume by default. A local
# folder or a volume, never a network share: SQLite needs shared memory for its
# write ahead log, and NFS or SMB cannot provide it.
DATA_DIR=/data

# ============================== Ports ===============================
# The page. Open http://localhost:3100 after `docker compose up -d`.
FRONTEND_PORT=3100
# The API, published on localhost only. The frontend reaches it inside the Docker
# network, so this port is needed only by host tools and by `npm run dev`.
BACKEND_PORT=8100

# Browser origins the API accepts. The frontend container is covered by the default.
#CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3100,http://localhost:3000
